---Specifies the settings for each trail.
---@class aws.cloudtrail.CreateTrailRequest
---@field Name aws.cloudtrail.String Specifies the name of the trail. The name must meet the following requirements:
---@field S3BucketName aws.cloudtrail.String Specifies the name of the Amazon S3 bucket designated for publishing log files. For information about bucket naming rules, see Bucket naming rules in the Amazon Simple Storage Service User Guide.
---@field S3KeyPrefix? aws.cloudtrail.String Specifies the Amazon S3 key prefix that comes after the name of the bucket you have designated for log file delivery. For more information, see Finding Your CloudTrail Log Files. The maximum length is 200 characters.
---@field SnsTopicName? aws.cloudtrail.String Specifies the name or ARN of the Amazon SNS topic defined for notification of log file delivery. The maximum length is 256 characters.
---@field IncludeGlobalServiceEvents? aws.cloudtrail.Boolean Specifies whether the trail is publishing events from global services such as IAM to the log files. Setting this value to true only delivers global service events to the trail if the trail is multi-Region or if the trail's home Region is the partition leader Region (for example, us-east-1).
---@field IsMultiRegionTrail? aws.cloudtrail.Boolean Specifies whether the trail is created in the current Region or in all Regions. The default is false, which creates a trail only in the Region where you are signed in. As a best practice, consider creating trails that log events in all Regions.
---@field EnableLogFileValidation? aws.cloudtrail.Boolean Specifies whether log file integrity validation is enabled. The default is false.
---@field CloudWatchLogsLogGroupArn? aws.cloudtrail.String Specifies a log group name using an Amazon Resource Name (ARN), a unique identifier that represents the log group to which CloudTrail logs will be delivered. You must use a log group that exists in your account.
---@field CloudWatchLogsRoleArn? aws.cloudtrail.String Specifies the role for the CloudWatch Logs endpoint to assume to write to a user's log group. You must use a role that exists in your account.
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.cloudtrail.String Specifies the KMS key ID to use to encrypt the logs and digest files delivered by CloudTrail. The value can be an alias name prefixed by alias/, a fully specified ARN to an alias, a fully specified ARN to a key, or a globally unique identifier.
---@field IsOrganizationTrail? aws.cloudtrail.Boolean Specifies whether the trail is created for all accounts in an organization in Organizations, or only for the current Amazon Web Services account. The default is false, and cannot be true unless the call is made on behalf of an Amazon Web Services account that is the management account or delegated administrator account for an organization in Organizations.
---@field TagsList? aws.cloudtrail.TagsList
---@field RecursiveLogging? aws.cloudtrail.Boolean Specifies whether recursive logging is enabled for the trail. If you set RecursiveLogging to false, CloudTrail suppresses events generated by CloudTrail when it delivers log files to your trail's destinations, including Amazon S3 and CloudWatch Logs. The default value is true.

