---@field EventSource aws.cloudtrail.EventSource The Amazon Web Services service to which the request was made, such as iam.amazonaws.com or s3.amazonaws.com.
---@field EventName aws.cloudtrail.EventName The name of the event, typically the Amazon Web Services API on which unusual levels of activity were recorded.
---@field InsightType aws.cloudtrail.InsightType|string The type of CloudTrail Insights event, which is either ApiCallRateInsight or ApiErrorRateInsight. The ApiCallRateInsight Insights type analyzes write-only management API calls that are aggregated per minute against a baseline API call volume. The ApiErrorRateInsight Insights type analyzes management API calls that result in error codes.
---@field ErrorCode? aws.cloudtrail.ErrorCode Conditionally required if the InsightType parameter is set to ApiErrorRateInsight.
---@field StartTime? aws.cloudtrail.Date Specifies, in UTC, the start time for time-series data. The value specified is inclusive; results include data points with the specified time stamp.
---@field EndTime? aws.cloudtrail.Date Specifies, in UTC, the end time for time-series data. The value specified is exclusive; results include data points up to the specified time stamp.
---@field Period? aws.cloudtrail.InsightsMetricPeriod Granularity of data to retrieve, in seconds. Valid values are 60, 300, and 3600. If you specify any other value, you will get an error. The default is 3600 seconds.
---@field DataType? aws.cloudtrail.InsightsMetricDataType|string Type of data points to return. Valid values are NonZeroData and FillWithZeros. The default is NonZeroData.
---@field MaxResults? aws.cloudtrail.InsightsMetricMaxResults The maximum number of data points to return. Valid values are integers from 1 to 21600. The default value is 21600.
---@field NextToken? aws.cloudtrail.InsightsMetricNextToken Returned if all datapoints can't be returned in a single call. For example, due to reaching MaxResults.

---@class aws.cloudtrail.ListInsightsMetricDataResponse
---@field TrailARN? aws.cloudtrail.String Specifies the ARN of the trail. This is only returned when Insights is enabled on a trail logging data events.
---@field EventSource? aws.cloudtrail.EventSource The Amazon Web Services service to which the request was made, such as iam.amazonaws.com or s3.amazonaws.com.
---@field EventName? aws.cloudtrail.EventName The name of the event, typically the Amazon Web Services API on which unusual levels of activity were recorded.
---@field InsightType? aws.cloudtrail.InsightType The type of CloudTrail Insights event, which is either ApiCallRateInsight or ApiErrorRateInsight. The ApiCallRateInsight Insights type analyzes write-only management API calls that are aggregated per minute against a baseline API call volume. The ApiErrorRateInsight Insights type analyzes management API calls that result in error codes.
---@field ErrorCode? aws.cloudtrail.ErrorCode Only returned if InsightType parameter was set to ApiErrorRateInsight.
---@field Timestamps? aws.cloudtrail.Timestamps List of timestamps at intervals corresponding to the specified time period.
---@field Values? aws.cloudtrail.InsightsMetricValues List of values representing the API call rate or error rate at each timestamp. The number of values is equal to the number of timestamps.
---@field NextToken? aws.cloudtrail.InsightsMetricNextToken Only returned if the full results could not be returned in a single query. You can set the NextToken parameter in the next request to this value to continue retrieval.

